# Moto G20 (java) recovery USB bring-up.
#
# Two stock facts force this file:
#  1. The Unisoc 4.14 kernel exposes no legacy android_usb f_ffs node
#     (/sys/class/android_usb/android0 carries only f_audio_source and
#     f_midi), so recovery's default sys.usb.configfs=0 path cannot attach
#     adbd. The configfs gadget path is proven on this device (stock normal
#     boot runs sys.usb.configfs=1 with /config/usb_gadget present).
#  2. Neither the stock cmdline nor any AOSP rc sets sys.usb.controller; on
#     stock it is set by a vendor component that does not run in recovery.
#     recovery's configfs handlers write /config/usb_gadget/g1/UDC from
#     ${sys.usb.controller}, so recovery needs it set explicitly.
#
# bootable/recovery's init.rc imports this file first; "on init" runs after
# both "on early-init" blocks and before "on fs", so the configfs branch of
# recovery's init.rc (gadget dirs, functionfs, ffs.adb) executes normally.
on init
    setprop sys.usb.configfs 1
    setprop sys.usb.controller musb-hdrc.0.auto

# Moto G20 (java) 2026-09-25: recovery touchscreen support (TWRP-model).
#
# The touch IC drivers are out-of-tree kernel modules; stock keeps them in
# the slotted socko partition (socko_a/socko_b — no unslotted by-name/socko)
# and normal boot insmods them from ${ro.vendor.ko.mount.point}/socko via
# vendor init.md.rc. Recovery parses no vendor rc and mounts no volume on
# boot, so /dev/input has NO touchscreen node and the recovery UI has no
# touch input — proven live 2026-09-25: /proc/bus/input/devices lists only
# keys/vibrator/headset in recovery. The G20 panel is an Ilitek
# ILI9882N/TXD_7806S — oreo_ili9882n.ko is the driver that registered the
# touch input device in normal boot (test14 console, ILITEK
# ili_input_register). FocalTech and Novatek modules follow TWRP's
# modules.load order as panel-variant fallbacks; a non-matching driver
# failing to probe is harmless.
#
# This build follows the known-good TWRP tree (Maluco-Test android_device_
# java-twrp, Recovery-11): the modules and the touch firmware ship inside
# recovery/root/vendor/ of THIS ramdisk (device/motorola/java/recovery/root/
# vendor/...). Nothing mounts the real vendor over it in recovery, so
# /vendor/lib/modules and /vendor/firmware (a ueventd firmware search path)
# resolve to the ramdisk copies. FIRMWARE IS MANDATORY: without
# ILITEK_FW_TXD_7806S the driver probes and registers the input device but
# the IC never reports touches (IRQ frozen, zero events — proven live);
# with it, full init runs (IRAM CRC ok) and touch works (190 multitouch
# events captured, UI confirmed).
on fs
    insmod /vendor/lib/modules/oreo_ili9882n.ko
    insmod /vendor/lib/modules/focaltech_touch.ko
    insmod /vendor/lib/modules/NVT_Touch.ko
